domain ADR0039:
  description "ADR-0039 revision 1. Accepted. V3-only immutable Battle binding and a narrow lifecycle with physical cutover."

problem P1:
  |
    The mainline ADR-0032 concerns authoring time boundaries, while preserved
    branch 77ed6a0 contains a different accepted ADR-0032 for V4 Battle binding.
    Its existing-Battle preservation clauses conflict for unfinished targets with the later owner decision to
    physically discard old unfinished battles. Current routes, replay and
    persistence distribute eligibility and can return or recreate a deleted Battle.

evidence OWNER:
  |
    The owner fixed new V3-versus-V3 battles, required battle-mechanics@3 only,
    immutable character revisions, physical disposal of old unfinished battles,
    readable finished history, and the narrow Battle domain/lifecycle direction.
    The owner requires minimum final program complexity and at most 30 minutes
    total migration work before proposing deletion or other alternatives.
    The current instruction prioritizes canonical PERT correction, then next work.

evidence UPSTREAM:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0010 requires immutable envelope binding and persisted atomic
    authoring activation. Accepted V3 authoring requirements v5 R18 requires exact
    candidate review and owner confirmation. Accepted ADR-0007 preserves physical
    provider-attempt accounting. Accepted cutover requirements v2 records the fixed
    owner behavior; ADR-0038 remains a separate Proposed Narration contract.

evidence CODE:
  |
    At 0585527 routes.ts creates deterministic Battle IDs from owner/scope/key/hash
    and returns cached HTTP responses before Battle existence checks.
    repositories/battles.ts writeBattle uses INSERT ON CONFLICT even for advances;
    its update-only fence cannot protect the missing-row insertion branch.
    db.ts has cascade and non-cascade narration tables, independent accounting
    rows and idempotency rows without a Battle foreign key.

evidence HISTORICAL:
  |
    Preserved 77ed6a01b9f6bea8d68702ab53839ef45ee78efd has accepted
    docs/adr/0032-bind-v3-characters-to-versioned-battles.think with SHA256
    0436026338e7decb420232950eaaaf9c11d3195b9b7834ad2f9ec4fe9199c625.
    It introduces V4 binding and full-consumer verification, retains V1-V3 meanings,
    says existing battles are not migrated, and says V2/dialogue-V3 continue unchanged.
    ADR-0010 Decision retains recorded legacy manifests; Compatibility keeps
    existing version-1 battles readable on embedded snapshots. Neither explicitly
    distinguishes finished from unfinished. Mainline ADR-0032 is a separate decision.

premise C1:
  |
    One pure BattleBinding contract plus narrow lifecycle use cases can share
    eligibility and retry invariants without relocating the engine into a giant
    class. Binding must cover the full execution/presentation tuple, not fixtures.
premise C2:
  |
    Physical deletion needs durable rejection of a deterministic old create ID,
    update-only advance saves, and worker/replay existence checks. A minimal
    deletion receipt stores only Battle ID and cutover identity, not old state.
    It also covers an old creation key whose HTTP receipt is missing. Merely
    deleting HTTP rows would permit deterministic recreation.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    A whole-engine class rewrite increases unrelated change surface. Per-route
    checks repeat rules. A narrow lifecycle retains engine/repository adapters.
    Retained inactive old Battle records add old state/read behavior. Minimal
    deletion receipts add a table and lookup but keep the old Battle body deleted.
    A new creation-key epoch could prevent replay but adds a client protocol and
    cutover-token distribution. Prefer minimal receipts and quiescent cutover.

decision D1 based_on P1, OWNER, UPSTREAM, HISTORICAL, C1:
  |
    Propose distinct BattleAssetManifestV4 for two V3 character generations and
    CharacterBattleCompilerInputsV4, preserving exact IDs/digests/snapshots and
    the complete dialogue/rule/compiler discriminator. Ready selection requires
    only battle-mechanics@3; schema/privacy validity remains independently checked.
    Creation reads accepted current generations; execution and all consumers use
    frozen inputs. V1-V3 retain historical meanings for finished read-only history.

decision D2 based_on CODE, C1, C2, OPTIONS:
  |
    Propose pure Battle eligibility/binding rules, small BattleLifecycle use cases
    and narrow storage/compiler/replay/narration ports. HTTP/SSE/action adapters
    share advance. Create exclusively inserts a fresh non-discarded ID; advance
    exclusively updates an existing row with revision and lease fence. Authorize
    existence/eligibility before any cached replay or narration delivery.
    Add minimal discarded Battle ID/cutover receipts atomically with deletion.
    Old create IDs return an unavailable response, including missing HTTP cache.
    Missing/deleted worker targets end normally without generation or publication.

decision D3 based_on OWNER, CODE, UPSTREAM, C2:
  |
    Propose one quiescent cutover: close game ingress and task dispatch, drain or
    stop old workers/revisions, freeze exact unfinished targets and recovery
    snapshot, transact deletion and receipts, read back, then expose V3-only.
    Delete Battle bodies, presentations, narration input/public events/outbox and
    HTTP replay bodies of targets. Retain immutable asset generations, finished
    history, provider accounting and balance accounting as historical audit.
    Resolve any retained active accounting run as failed after draining. Accounting
    data supplies no continuation. A late already-sent provider completion may
    settle accounting, but creates no new provider call or public Battle output.
    Rollback before exposure restores a coherent snapshot with ingress closed;
    after exposure use a reviewed forward recovery to preserve new V3 work.

decision D4 based_on OWNER, UPSTREAM, HISTORICAL, D1:
  |
    On exact acceptance, for cutover-requirement R3 targets only (created before
    cutover and not finished at cutover), replace ADR-0010 Decision's existing
    legacy-manifest retention and Compatibility's existing-Battle readability,
    and preserved ADR-0032 Decision 4's non-migration/preservation plus its
    Consequences' unchanged continuation, with physical disposal. Finished history,
    immutable binding and authoring obligations retain their recorded meanings.
    Current mainline authoring-time ADR-0032 is unchanged. Record this historical
    collision by path/hash, not by replacing its unrelated file.
    Finished-history migration, if required, shares the owner's 30-minute total
    budget with ADR-0038; overrun routes a concrete alternative to the owner.
    The first V3 trial does not implement or accept ADR-0038 Fragment semantics.

decision VERIFY based_on D1, D2, D3, D4:
  |
    vt102 proves V3 creation, immutable full-consumer execution/reload/retry.
    vt109 independently follows already Accepted R18 and ADR-0010/0014 to prove
    exact review/confirmation and atomic activation across storage contracts; its
    implementation does not wait for this ADR acceptance. vt110 proves deletion, deterministic old-key rejection, stale save
    conflict, HTTP/SSE/action/state replay, delayed worker and read-only finished
    history. vt103 exercises the real local user path. Stage inventory, exact
    release, interruption/recovery budget and data authority belong to vt104-vt108.
    Schema tests or a fixture importer alone do not complete these obligations.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-29 the owner explicitly accepted the exact requirement v2,
    ADR0039 revision 1 and lifecycle design v2 package presented in this chat.
    The answer was: この候補一式を採用して進める（推奨）.
    docs/evidence/cc319-owner-acceptance-2026-09-29.md preserves the four
    submitted SHA256 identities and the limited D4 replacement scope.
    The subsequent handoff instruction keeps vt102 suspended for continuation.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    Record the already accepted ADR0039 revision 1 package and scope documented
    in the existing OWNER_ACCEPTANCE evidence and cc319 acceptance record.
    D1-D4 and VERIFY retain their accepted meanings. This receipt projection
    grants no new execution authority, does not resume suspended vt102, and
    does not authorize Stage, production, data operations or a discarded trial.
